# Following an external clock (EXT). PLAY starts the piece at once, at the tempo in store (Transport.swift: tick 0
# at the press, until the pulses lead). MIDI Start (FA) from the TRS jack starts it the same way; then each clock
# pulse (F8) is 40 ticks, the clock runs between pulses at the last beat's rate (24 pulses 20 ms apart: 2 ticks a
# ms, 125 BPM, the tempo it reports) and never past the next pulse. The pulses stop (a router unplugged): after
# 500 ms the clock runs on at the same rate, playing; MIDI Stop (FC) stops it. Clock from USB is not followed while
# the input is TRS alone, before the start or while running, and nothing of the clock goes out (the FM-1 never
# sends a clock it follows).
proj template full 2477861893
rt sync ext
rt port TRS
# PLAY with no clock coming: the Full ensemble's 96 BPM (1.536 ticks a ms) from the press (ms 1)
tap PLAY
wait 920
expect playing 1
expect tick 1534
expect bpm 96
expect tick_rate 1536
expect midi_out >10
# then a clock from the jack (a DAW started after the FM-1): its first pulse comes long after tick 0, so the clock
# takes up from the next multiple of 40 and never steps back; the notes keep going out
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
midi TRS F8
wait 18
expect tick 2038
expect midi_out >29
midi TRS F8
wait 18
