# the notes went out on the followed clock; the 96th pulse is tick 3800, 19 ms ago (a "midi" line runs 2 ms): 38
# ticks on, then held short of the next: after FA and N pulses the tick is in 40 (N - 1) ... 40 N - 1, no lead
expect midi_out >20
expect tick_rate 2000
expect bpm 125
expect tick 3838
expect tick >3799
expect tick <3840
wait 10
expect tick 3839
# no pulse: held on 3839 to 500 ms after the last, then on at 2 ticks per ms (1529 ms of the 2 s: 3839 + 3058)
wait 2000
expect playing 1
expect tick_rate 2000
expect bpm 125
expect tick 6897
expect clocks_out 0
# the pulses again: on from the tick reached (6899: the pulse is 6920, the next multiple of 40), never back
midi TRS F8
expect tick 6922
expect tick_rate 2000
wait 18
midi TRS F8
expect tick 6962
midi TRS FC
expect playing 0
wait 1
expect sounding 0
expect clocks_out 0
# stopped, the tempo shown is the transport's, as on the Mac (UIState's liveBPM, Transport.currentBPM): the 125
# followed, not the project's 96, and still after Sync INT, which keeps it (Transport.setSyncMode), as PLAY runs it
expect bpm_shown 125
proj sync int
expect bpm 125
expect bpm_shown 125
expect tick_rate 2000
proj sync ext
# a SAVE made while playing in EXT is written after MIDI Stop, once what the stop sends has gone out (a flash write
# stops everything for a moment: the offs would wait behind it): 128 notes sounding, their offs 8 ms on the wire
tap PLAY
wait 300
tap SAVE
expect save_pending 1
rt burst 128
wait 8
expect sounding15 >100
midi TRS FC
wait 40
expect playing 0
expect save_pending 0
expect store_writes 1
expect save_unsent 0
expect sounding 0
# the tempo in store is the project's after a change that rebuilds the transport (the Mac's rebuildTransport keeps
# the sync, its new transport has the project's tempo): Sync EXT from the project, then Ambient drift (72 BPM) chosen
# while stopped; PLAY with no clock runs at 72 (1.152 ticks a ms), not at the 125 followed before
proj sync ext
proj template ambient 1
expect bpm 72
expect tick_rate 1152
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 1
expect bpm 72
expect tick_rate 1152
tap PLAY
# saved with EXT, after a restart: the saved tempo, not that of the Full ensemble the transport starts on
save
reboot
expect sync 1
expect bpm 72
expect tick_rate 1152
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect playing 1
expect tick_rate 1152
tap PLAY
# an FC that the tick takes between an FA and the main loop's start (its interrupt between app_loop's look and the
# start's lock) takes the FA back: nothing starts, nothing free-runs while the master is stopped
racefc
midi TRS FA
expect playing 0
wait 500
expect playing 0
expect tick 0
expect clocks_out 0
